1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:06,360
The Viet Cong's rapid transit system, a labyrinth of interlocking tunnels, bunkers and barracks,

2
00:00:06,361 --> 00:00:11,200
an underground city supporting hospitals, classrooms and command centers.

3
00:00:11,201 --> 00:00:15,360
This maze stretched as far south as Saigon and allowed the North Vietnamese to strike

4
00:00:15,361 --> 00:00:18,200
at the heart of U.S. operations in Vietnam.

5
00:00:18,201 --> 00:00:21,440
Now, the Tunnels of Vietnam on Modern Marvels.

6
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:40,240
It was here in rural South Vietnam that America and her allies met their darkest hour.

7
00:00:40,241 --> 00:00:48,660
This tropical land of rice paddies, small villages, and peasant farmers soon turned into a living hell

8
00:00:48,661 --> 00:00:54,320
for the GIs as they tried to wage war against a dedicated and determined enemy.

9
00:00:54,321 --> 00:00:59,320
To combat America's superior firepower and complete control

10
00:00:59,420 --> 00:01:04,060
of the air, the Viet Cong adopted a brilliant strategy.

11
00:01:04,160 --> 00:01:05,700
At the heart of their resistance,

12
00:01:05,800 --> 00:01:08,960
a deadly spider's web of fiercely defended tunnels

13
00:01:09,060 --> 00:01:11,800
and subterranean bunkers under the rice fields

14
00:01:11,900 --> 00:01:14,580
and jungles of South Vietnam.

15
00:01:14,680 --> 00:01:17,380
The communist fighters literally lived, ate,

16
00:01:17,480 --> 00:01:19,920
and slept under the battlefield.

17
00:01:20,020 --> 00:01:24,320
They had hospitals, classrooms, and armament workshops.

18
00:01:24,321 --> 00:01:26,960
From these fortified nests, the guerrillas sprung

19
00:01:27,020 --> 00:01:28,260
their deadly ambushes.

20
00:01:31,060 --> 00:01:34,200
But a courageous few American and Australian foot soldiers,

21
00:01:34,260 --> 00:01:37,800
the Tunnel Rats, dared to staunch the enemy tide.

22
00:01:37,860 --> 00:01:41,440
It was their terrifying task to chase the enemy down

23
00:01:41,500 --> 00:01:45,600
into their booby-trapped retreat.

24
00:01:45,680 --> 00:01:49,020
And you get down in a tunnel and start closing in on you

25
00:01:49,080 --> 00:01:50,840
or you hear noises and you start shooting

26
00:01:50,920 --> 00:01:54,320
and you can get cranked up real easy and lose it.

27
00:01:54,321 --> 00:02:01,320
and probably make you go insane if you ain't not careful.

28
00:02:01,420 --> 00:02:04,600
When you expanded your lungs, when you took a breath,

29
00:02:04,700 --> 00:02:06,340
you were kind of wedged in.

30
00:02:06,440 --> 00:02:08,400
Now, if you can picture yourself being stuck,

31
00:02:08,500 --> 00:02:10,040
if there was a cave in or something,

32
00:02:10,140 --> 00:02:12,840
I can't imagine a worse way to die.

33
00:02:12,940 --> 00:02:15,400
The tunnel rats would soon distinguish themselves

34
00:02:15,500 --> 00:02:20,740
for their uncommon valor and selfless commitment to duty.

35
00:02:20,840 --> 00:02:22,120
You took pride in what you did.

36
00:02:22,121 --> 00:02:23,620
There wasn't very many of us.

37
00:02:23,720 --> 00:02:27,360
But if you did it well, you know you did something worthwhile.

38
00:02:27,460 --> 00:02:30,160
Because whatever you unearthed, whatever you uncovered,

39
00:02:30,260 --> 00:02:33,260
whether it be intelligence, maps,

40
00:02:33,360 --> 00:02:36,160
we get the edge on the enemy.

41
00:02:36,260 --> 00:02:39,100
The most dangerous part would be psyching up

42
00:02:39,200 --> 00:02:40,640
to get into the tunnel.

43
00:02:40,740 --> 00:02:44,180
That was the part that was really the most frightening,

44
00:02:44,280 --> 00:02:50,180
because you didn't know what you were getting into.

45
00:02:50,181 --> 00:02:53,420
When the US and Allied troops first arrived in Vietnam

46
00:02:53,520 --> 00:02:56,480
in the early 1960s, they had no idea

47
00:02:56,580 --> 00:02:59,220
that the enemy were under their very feet.

48
00:02:59,320 --> 00:03:01,320
On the surface, the tunnel entrances

49
00:03:01,420 --> 00:03:03,420
were carefully camouflaged.

50
00:03:03,520 --> 00:03:07,840
VC guerrillas appeared and disappeared down them at will.

51
00:03:07,940 --> 00:03:09,840
They were so well concealed.

52
00:03:09,940 --> 00:03:12,240
I mean, we probably walked over thousands of them,

53
00:03:12,340 --> 00:03:15,480
never knew it, especially in the Coochie area.

54
00:03:15,580 --> 00:03:20,140
That's where the majority of all the people

55
00:03:20,180 --> 00:03:24,080
tunnels were. The small town of Cu Chi,

56
00:03:24,081 --> 00:03:27,780
just 50 miles north of Saigon, was at the heart of the Viet Cong's

57
00:03:27,781 --> 00:03:32,220
secret network. By 1965, the system snaked nearly

58
00:03:32,221 --> 00:03:35,760
200 miles under villages, huts, and fields.

59
00:03:35,761 --> 00:03:38,960
It weaved from the Ho Chi Minh Trail in the north to the gates

60
00:03:38,961 --> 00:03:42,660
of Saigon in the south.

61
00:03:42,661 --> 00:03:48,340
Under the battlefield was a system of tunnels connecting

62
00:03:48,341 --> 00:03:52,680
communities from village to village.

63
00:03:52,681 --> 00:03:56,380
This was not the first time tunnels have been used in war.

64
00:03:56,381 --> 00:03:58,760
In fact, tunnels and underground fortifications

65
00:03:58,761 --> 00:04:01,440
had been used for thousands of years.

66
00:04:01,441 --> 00:04:03,800
Among the first troops with a specific mission

67
00:04:03,801 --> 00:04:06,900
to search and destroy the enemy's underground bunkers

68
00:04:06,901 --> 00:04:10,600
were British sappers in World War I, and most famously,

69
00:04:10,601 --> 00:04:13,420
the US Marines in World War II.

70
00:04:13,421 --> 00:04:16,580
As early as 1943, the Japanese dug

71
00:04:16,581 --> 00:04:20,480
confounding subterranean defenses on the coral atolls

72
00:04:20,481 --> 00:04:22,560
of the Central Pacific.

73
00:04:22,561 --> 00:04:24,620
Penetrating the caves and hidden bunkers

74
00:04:24,621 --> 00:04:27,960
on the many islands like Saipan, Peleliu, Iwo Jima,

75
00:04:27,961 --> 00:04:31,760
and Okinawa became a challenging and dangerous task

76
00:04:31,761 --> 00:04:35,860
for these first US troops to be called tunnel rats.

77
00:04:35,861 --> 00:04:40,500
We developed, this took us some time and a little bit of blood,

78
00:04:40,501 --> 00:04:45,100
we developed techniques to deal with these things.

79
00:04:45,101 --> 00:04:49,360
Above all, this meant ceiling entrances, ceiling exits,

80
00:04:49,361 --> 00:04:51,580
going in with flamethrowers, frankly,

81
00:04:51,581 --> 00:04:54,120
entombing or killing the people inside.

82
00:04:54,121 --> 00:04:55,980
And you were able to do this.

83
00:04:55,981 --> 00:04:59,160
In 1946 in Vietnam, the Viet Minh,

84
00:04:59,161 --> 00:05:01,340
as the resistance fighters were then called,

85
00:05:01,341 --> 00:05:03,940
began digging tunnels and underground bunkers

86
00:05:03,941 --> 00:05:06,340
to fight the French, who returned to Vietnam

87
00:05:06,341 --> 00:05:09,880
after World War II to reoccupy the former colony

88
00:05:09,881 --> 00:05:13,600
they called Indochina.

89
00:05:13,601 --> 00:05:18,040
In the spring of 1954, the Viet Minh defeated the French

90
00:05:18,041 --> 00:05:21,900
in the celebrated battle for Diem Bien Phu.

91
00:05:21,901 --> 00:05:26,280
It spelt the end for the French and their empirical aspirations.

92
00:05:26,281 --> 00:05:30,420
For the next 10 years, while the Army of South Vietnam, or ARVN,

93
00:05:30,421 --> 00:05:34,080
and the Saigon government were mired in corruption and coups,

94
00:05:34,081 --> 00:05:37,660
the communist guerrillas now called Viet Cong, or VC,

95
00:05:37,661 --> 00:05:42,020
took control of rural South Vietnam.

96
00:05:42,021 --> 00:05:45,340
When they arrived in 1965, the US armies,

97
00:05:45,341 --> 00:05:47,820
including the 1st and 25th divisions,

98
00:05:47,821 --> 00:05:50,160
stepped into a bear trap.

99
00:05:50,161 --> 00:05:53,360
The enemy, battle-hardened communist guerrillas.

100
00:05:58,860 --> 00:06:02,040
The Americans thought they could win the war easily,

101
00:06:03,560 --> 00:06:06,620
but in reality, it wasn't that simple.

102
00:06:12,020 --> 00:06:17,020
When we lost in combat, we did not take it as a loss.

103
00:06:17,021 --> 00:06:20,020
It gave us other presence and strength,

104
00:06:20,021 --> 00:06:23,020
which we would take into the next battle.

105
00:06:25,020 --> 00:06:28,020
From the hidden underground bunkers and spider holes,

106
00:06:28,021 --> 00:06:31,020
the Viet Cong guerrillas sprung devastating ambushes

107
00:06:31,021 --> 00:06:35,020
and stealthy night attacks that inflicted horrific casualties

108
00:06:35,021 --> 00:06:37,020
on American forces.

109
00:06:37,021 --> 00:06:39,020
You'd be walking through an area,

110
00:06:39,021 --> 00:06:41,020
and you're really thinking there's going to be a bunker over here,

111
00:06:41,021 --> 00:06:43,020
and there might be a sniper up in this tree

112
00:06:43,021 --> 00:06:44,360
and that kind of thing.

113
00:06:44,361 --> 00:06:46,620
But most of the danger came from walking

114
00:06:46,621 --> 00:06:48,620
to an area that was infest of these tunnels

115
00:06:48,621 --> 00:06:50,760
and what we call spider holes, just small,

116
00:06:50,761 --> 00:06:53,760
maybe just big around holes that these guys could pop up

117
00:06:53,761 --> 00:06:57,780
out of, take a shot, hit a guy in the back, pop back down.

118
00:06:57,781 --> 00:07:00,680
The young American and Allied soldiers on patrol

119
00:07:00,681 --> 00:07:03,680
in the thick jungle canopy of South Vietnam

120
00:07:03,681 --> 00:07:07,020
were left chasing shadows in an alien environment

121
00:07:07,021 --> 00:07:09,020
where violence and fear characterized

122
00:07:09,021 --> 00:07:12,060
characterized their daily existence.

123
00:07:12,160 --> 00:07:15,260
You dreaded being in a jungle where you can't see.

124
00:07:15,360 --> 00:07:16,660
It was scary.

125
00:07:16,760 --> 00:07:18,760
There were times where some jungle parts were,

126
00:07:18,860 --> 00:07:21,560
even at 12 o'clock noon, you'd have to use a flashlight

127
00:07:21,660 --> 00:07:24,360
to see because it was that dark.

128
00:07:24,460 --> 00:07:25,640
Everybody was the same.

129
00:07:25,740 --> 00:07:26,940
Everybody depended on each other.

130
00:07:27,040 --> 00:07:30,580
You know, sure, we got scared as hell sometimes,

131
00:07:30,680 --> 00:07:34,440
and sometimes you get so damn scared you couldn't move.

132
00:07:34,540 --> 00:07:36,740
To survive the horror of combat,

133
00:07:36,741 --> 00:07:41,740
soldiers quickly learned to suppress their emotions.

134
00:07:41,840 --> 00:07:44,820
On Operation Crimp, I think the first day

135
00:07:44,920 --> 00:07:49,680
there was four blokes killed, and I walked past their bodies

136
00:07:49,780 --> 00:07:53,860
and felt nothing, absolutely nothing.

137
00:07:53,960 --> 00:07:56,500
The Viet Cong became brilliantly adept

138
00:07:56,600 --> 00:07:58,800
at making savage booby traps.

139
00:07:58,900 --> 00:08:01,200
Some devices were brutally simple.

140
00:08:01,300 --> 00:08:03,800
When a trooper stepped onto one of these man traps,

141
00:08:03,801 --> 00:08:07,640
the wooden spikes impaled and incapacitated him.

142
00:08:07,740 --> 00:08:09,680
The guerrillas became especially skilled

143
00:08:09,780 --> 00:08:12,480
at turning unexploded American ordnance

144
00:08:12,580 --> 00:08:15,440
into devastating booby traps.

145
00:08:15,540 --> 00:08:17,420
Most of the time we found booby traps,

146
00:08:17,520 --> 00:08:21,080
it was because somebody triggered it.

147
00:08:21,180 --> 00:08:24,960
Infantryman and soon-to-be tunnel rat Gary Schooler

148
00:08:25,060 --> 00:08:28,500
remembers vividly his first patrol in the Hobo Woods,

149
00:08:28,600 --> 00:08:30,920
just east of the Iron Triangle.

150
00:08:31,020 --> 00:08:33,800
This is the first time I saw anybody killed.

151
00:08:33,801 --> 00:08:35,800
my first day out.

152
00:08:35,900 --> 00:08:37,400
And some guy sat down.

153
00:08:37,500 --> 00:08:38,540
We call them stick mines.

154
00:08:38,640 --> 00:08:40,340
It's a vertical bamboo stick.

155
00:08:40,440 --> 00:08:41,540
You can tilt it.

156
00:08:41,640 --> 00:08:42,640
You don't even have to step on it.

157
00:08:42,740 --> 00:08:43,740
You just tilt it, and it goes off.

158
00:08:43,840 --> 00:08:45,340
And then there's horrible screaming.

159
00:08:45,440 --> 00:08:46,540
It's a real high shriek.

160
00:08:46,640 --> 00:08:48,240
It's just ear piercing.

161
00:08:48,340 --> 00:08:49,440
And so you don't forget it.

162
00:08:49,540 --> 00:08:50,560
When you hear that sound, you don't forget it.

163
00:08:50,660 --> 00:08:53,860
You know there's movie travel.

164
00:08:53,960 --> 00:08:59,560
In October 1965, 68 Australian engineers, or sappers,

165
00:08:59,660 --> 00:09:03,200
from three field troops arrived in Vietnam primarily

166
00:09:03,201 --> 00:09:06,900
to help locate and disarm the booby traps.

167
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:09,200
However, they soon made a critical discovery

168
00:09:09,300 --> 00:09:11,840
that changed the course of the war.

169
00:09:11,940 --> 00:09:18,040
25-year-old Captain Alex Sandy McGregor led the way.

170
00:09:18,140 --> 00:09:21,660
We came across this tunnel within a village, which

171
00:09:21,760 --> 00:09:23,260
was an enemy village.

172
00:09:23,360 --> 00:09:26,460
What happened was that I went down the tunnel.

173
00:09:26,560 --> 00:09:30,300
And I can remember my sergeant, my staff sergeant,

174
00:09:30,301 --> 00:09:35,300
actually holding my legs with a rope

175
00:09:35,400 --> 00:09:38,540
because I went down head first.

176
00:09:38,640 --> 00:09:39,940
This first tunnel turned out

177
00:09:40,040 --> 00:09:42,940
to be a relatively short escape tunnel from a village hut.

178
00:09:43,040 --> 00:09:45,640
It would, however, be dwarfed by an incredible discovery

179
00:09:45,740 --> 00:09:46,960
on their next mission.

180
00:09:47,060 --> 00:09:50,060
The Australians were about to find the enemy's massive secret

181
00:09:50,160 --> 00:09:52,060
tunnel labyrinth, but their success

182
00:09:52,160 --> 00:09:54,960
would come at a deadly price.

183
00:09:55,060 --> 00:09:58,200
Many innovative weapons, including the Claymore mines,

184
00:09:58,201 --> 00:10:00,840
were introduced to combat during the Vietnam War.

185
00:10:00,940 --> 00:10:04,540
Among them were the F-4s, the AH-1G Huey Cobra,

186
00:10:04,640 --> 00:10:05,600
and the gunship.

187
00:10:11,540 --> 00:10:16,180
On January 7, 1966, American and Allied forces

188
00:10:16,280 --> 00:10:19,080
under the direction of General William Westmoreland

189
00:10:19,180 --> 00:10:21,420
launched a massive attack, spearheaded

190
00:10:21,520 --> 00:10:24,460
by the pride of America's military, the 1st Infantry

191
00:10:24,560 --> 00:10:27,060
Division.

192
00:10:27,061 --> 00:10:30,000
The strike was aimed at the heart of the Viet Cong war machine

193
00:10:30,100 --> 00:10:31,800
in South Vietnam.

194
00:10:31,900 --> 00:10:34,800
They moved into the Ho Bo woods just east

195
00:10:34,900 --> 00:10:35,900
of the Iron Triangle.

196
00:10:39,200 --> 00:10:41,900
Helicopters, tanks, armored personnel carriers,

197
00:10:42,000 --> 00:10:46,420
and more than 8,000 men joined the battle.

198
00:10:46,520 --> 00:10:48,620
In one huge blow, America's leaders

199
00:10:48,720 --> 00:10:52,720
planned to find and destroy the Viet Cong Politico headquarters

200
00:10:52,820 --> 00:10:54,420
and effectively end the war.

201
00:10:57,060 --> 00:11:00,860
The Australian engineers of Three Field Troop

202
00:11:00,960 --> 00:11:05,100
were assigned to support the crack 173rd Airborne Brigade.

203
00:11:05,200 --> 00:11:09,800
They deployed from their base of Yinhua, just east of Saigon.

204
00:11:09,900 --> 00:11:13,140
The Australians headed for the south edge of the Hobo Woods.

205
00:11:13,240 --> 00:11:15,540
If all went according to plan, the enemy

206
00:11:15,640 --> 00:11:18,180
would be swept down towards them.

207
00:11:18,280 --> 00:11:20,420
Then the Australians would cut them off,

208
00:11:20,520 --> 00:11:22,320
but the plan backfired.

209
00:11:22,420 --> 00:11:27,060
The enemy was already waiting when they landed.

210
00:11:27,061 --> 00:11:32,020
As soon as we landed, I knew there was something up.

211
00:11:32,021 --> 00:11:33,860
There were shots coming out.

212
00:11:33,861 --> 00:11:36,020
There were guns going off.

213
00:11:36,021 --> 00:11:37,900
We were being mortared at that time.

214
00:11:40,820 --> 00:11:45,180
The thing that no training will ever prepare you for

215
00:11:45,181 --> 00:11:48,580
is the sound, the sound and the smell.

216
00:11:51,020 --> 00:11:53,780
The noise is indescribable.

217
00:11:53,781 --> 00:11:56,100
And of course, the other thing is that time really

218
00:11:56,101 --> 00:12:00,340
and things become very, very vivid whilst every year in action.

219
00:12:02,500 --> 00:12:05,780
In the midst of the chaos, an Australian infantryman

220
00:12:05,880 --> 00:12:09,420
spotted Viet Cong snipers firing from slits in what

221
00:12:09,520 --> 00:12:11,420
looked like an anthill.

222
00:12:11,520 --> 00:12:15,120
He crawled towards it and slung a grenade into the mound.

223
00:12:15,220 --> 00:12:18,360
He then called the engineers of three field troops.

224
00:12:20,500 --> 00:12:22,420
The Aussie sappers were ready.

225
00:12:22,520 --> 00:12:24,620
They had already devised a technique

226
00:12:24,621 --> 00:12:26,720
a technique to deal with the tunnels.

227
00:12:26,820 --> 00:12:29,720
They first blew the top off to reveal an entrance.

228
00:12:29,820 --> 00:12:32,160
And then they used an industrial air blower

229
00:12:32,260 --> 00:12:36,360
called a Mighty Might and blew smoke down the hole.

230
00:12:36,460 --> 00:12:40,400
Then what we did was we blew down tear gas.

231
00:12:40,500 --> 00:12:42,040
The smoke was to find entrances.

232
00:12:42,140 --> 00:12:45,980
The tear gas was to clear the tunnel of enemy

233
00:12:46,080 --> 00:12:47,180
as far as we could.

234
00:12:47,280 --> 00:12:50,380
And then our boys wearing gas masks,

235
00:12:50,480 --> 00:12:54,380
torch in one hand, bayonet in the other.

236
00:12:54,381 --> 00:12:56,840
going down the tunnel.

237
00:12:56,940 --> 00:12:58,860
The tunnel was empty.

238
00:12:58,960 --> 00:13:02,420
They then prepared explosives to destroy it.

239
00:13:02,520 --> 00:13:04,360
They skillfully placed the charges

240
00:13:04,460 --> 00:13:07,320
to make the maximum impact.

241
00:13:07,420 --> 00:13:10,760
The charges that were used were all big.

242
00:13:10,860 --> 00:13:12,760
Military demolitions is like that.

243
00:13:12,860 --> 00:13:15,340
You make sure that the job's done properly the first time.

244
00:13:15,440 --> 00:13:17,500
So the charges were big.

245
00:13:17,600 --> 00:13:20,840
Less than a mile away, another tunnel had been found.

246
00:13:20,940 --> 00:13:23,340
Aussie sapper Ray Forrester and his partner

247
00:13:23,341 --> 00:13:26,180
and his partner were sent to investigate.

248
00:13:26,181 --> 00:13:27,340
I was scared the whole time.

249
00:13:27,341 --> 00:13:29,240
I won't even deny it.

250
00:13:29,241 --> 00:13:31,680
And inside, it was an eerie silence.

251
00:13:31,681 --> 00:13:36,020
You could kind of hear yourself breathing.

252
00:13:36,021 --> 00:13:40,600
Yeah, it was just very eerie.

253
00:13:40,601 --> 00:13:43,360
It was all slime on the walls.

254
00:13:43,361 --> 00:13:44,920
Whatever you touch was slimy.

255
00:13:44,921 --> 00:13:51,440
And it just felt like pigs to the slaughter,

256
00:13:51,441 --> 00:13:53,940
because it's just rolling around in the mud.

257
00:13:53,941 --> 00:13:56,180
While simple tunnels and underground bunkers

258
00:13:56,181 --> 00:13:58,620
had been found before, the ones discovered

259
00:13:58,621 --> 00:14:03,800
during Operation Crimp were on a massive scale never seen before.

260
00:14:03,801 --> 00:14:05,960
They found whole gorilla encampments

261
00:14:05,961 --> 00:14:10,140
underground, bunkers connected by tiny passageways.

262
00:14:10,141 --> 00:14:13,440
There were chambers that stored arms and food.

263
00:14:13,441 --> 00:14:16,820
They had sleeping quarters and areas to treat the wounded.

264
00:14:16,821 --> 00:14:20,200
The tunnel rats found hidden trap doors laced with booby

265
00:14:20,201 --> 00:14:23,700
that led to even deeper levels and more chambers.

266
00:14:23,800 --> 00:14:26,840
They had uncovered the Viet Cong's secret underground

267
00:14:26,940 --> 00:14:27,640
fortifications.

268
00:14:31,340 --> 00:14:34,240
When General Westmoreland was informed of the find,

269
00:14:34,340 --> 00:14:37,760
he ordered all tunnels be searched for men, intelligence,

270
00:14:37,860 --> 00:14:39,260
arms, and supplies.

271
00:14:39,360 --> 00:14:42,060
Then they were to be destroyed.

272
00:14:42,160 --> 00:14:47,260
The tunnel rats, driven by duty and courage, went to work.

273
00:14:47,360 --> 00:14:50,180
When they found trap doors, they took even more

274
00:14:50,200 --> 00:14:52,840
in case it was armed with a booby trap.

275
00:14:52,940 --> 00:14:54,140
You'd use your fingers.

276
00:14:54,240 --> 00:14:56,340
You virtually went down and kissed it.

277
00:14:56,440 --> 00:14:57,900
That's how close you got, you know,

278
00:14:58,000 --> 00:15:01,140
just to make sure that you didn't miss anything.

279
00:15:01,240 --> 00:15:05,340
You can't miss anything, so you always just checked

280
00:15:05,440 --> 00:15:06,960
and double checked.

281
00:15:07,060 --> 00:15:11,860
On day two of Operation Crimp, on January 8, 1966,

282
00:15:11,960 --> 00:15:14,560
three field troops returned to the Hobo Woods

283
00:15:14,660 --> 00:15:17,860
and parachuted into a hornet's nest.

284
00:15:17,861 --> 00:15:21,460
Incredibly, they landed on a VC tunnel.

285
00:15:21,560 --> 00:15:23,760
What they unearthed in it almost changed

286
00:15:23,860 --> 00:15:25,660
the course of the war.

287
00:15:25,760 --> 00:15:27,500
What we landed on was the headquarters

288
00:15:27,600 --> 00:15:29,000
of the Cholonghain area.

289
00:15:29,100 --> 00:15:31,500
We actually even pulled out the hit list, right,

290
00:15:31,600 --> 00:15:34,940
that the Viet Cong had of the senior officers in Saigon

291
00:15:35,040 --> 00:15:37,520
in the order that they were going to be hit.

292
00:15:37,620 --> 00:15:40,520
The VC hit list whetted their curiosity.

293
00:15:40,620 --> 00:15:43,620
The tunnel rats had unearthed a gold mine.

294
00:15:43,720 --> 00:15:45,980
They descended deeper, down three levels,

295
00:15:45,981 --> 00:15:50,620
on three levels, but stopped before opening a trapdoor.

296
00:15:50,621 --> 00:15:53,220
Had they gone through that trapdoor,

297
00:15:53,221 --> 00:15:57,060
we would have unleashed hell, because that was the only

298
00:15:57,061 --> 00:16:02,820
entrance into the heavy headquarters for the Saigon

299
00:16:02,821 --> 00:16:04,360
area.

300
00:16:04,361 --> 00:16:08,200
One trapdoor, and we could have changed the whole war.

301
00:16:08,201 --> 00:16:11,100
Really, it's terrifying to know that there were that many people

302
00:16:11,101 --> 00:16:13,100
down below us.

303
00:16:13,101 --> 00:16:17,040
But also, I don't know what would have happened,

304
00:16:17,041 --> 00:16:19,740
to be quite honest with you.

305
00:16:19,741 --> 00:16:21,540
They only realized how close they were

306
00:16:21,541 --> 00:16:26,880
to the enemy headquarters after the war was over.

307
00:16:26,881 --> 00:16:30,740
Tragically, Operation Crimp also marked the first tunnel rat

308
00:16:30,741 --> 00:16:32,060
casualty.

309
00:16:32,061 --> 00:16:35,140
Corporal Bob Bartell got trapped in a small tunnel

310
00:16:35,141 --> 00:16:37,240
filled with smoke.

311
00:16:37,241 --> 00:16:40,420
Ray Forster went down the tunnel to try and pull his friend

312
00:16:40,421 --> 00:16:42,700
out of the tunnel shaft.

313
00:16:42,701 --> 00:16:45,400
I must have gone down a few times.

314
00:16:45,401 --> 00:16:47,140
I just couldn't move him, couldn't budge him.

315
00:16:47,141 --> 00:16:49,880
He was just stuck at the bottom of the trapdoor.

316
00:16:49,881 --> 00:16:53,800
I remember trying to dig out the tunnel entrance.

317
00:16:53,801 --> 00:16:58,660
But again, that really wasn't satisfactory.

318
00:16:58,661 --> 00:17:01,120
Yeah, I don't know at that stage.

319
00:17:01,121 --> 00:17:04,820
I guess later on he was dead, but I didn't know that at the time.

320
00:17:04,821 --> 00:17:07,980
I thought I could try and get him out.

321
00:17:07,981 --> 00:17:14,020
When I finally had to give in, I went back up top.

322
00:17:14,021 --> 00:17:15,020
And um...

323
00:17:21,820 --> 00:17:24,420
Ray Forrester was unable to save his friend

324
00:17:24,421 --> 00:17:26,740
and reluctantly, following orders,

325
00:17:26,741 --> 00:17:27,740
returned to the surface.

326
00:17:31,820 --> 00:17:34,300
They realized that the smoke from the Mighty Might

327
00:17:34,301 --> 00:17:37,180
had sucked all the oxygen out of the tunnel,

328
00:17:37,181 --> 00:17:41,480
and Corporal Bartel suffocated to death.

329
00:17:41,481 --> 00:17:44,420
Operation Crimp was ended five days later,

330
00:17:44,421 --> 00:17:49,160
and American and Australian forces retreated.

331
00:17:49,161 --> 00:17:52,300
With the incredible discovery of a vast enemy underground

332
00:17:52,301 --> 00:17:54,460
network, however, more tunnel rats

333
00:17:54,461 --> 00:17:56,240
would be needed to risk their lives

334
00:17:56,241 --> 00:17:58,400
and volunteer for this deadly mission.

335
00:18:02,280 --> 00:18:06,100
Westmoreland requested an additional 206,000 troops

336
00:18:06,101 --> 00:18:09,400
the height of the Tet Offensive in 1968.

337
00:18:09,401 --> 00:18:13,140
This top secret request was codenamed Operation Complete

338
00:18:13,141 --> 00:18:13,841
Victory.

339
00:18:17,760 --> 00:18:22,680
January 1966, the 25th Tropic Lightning Infantry Division

340
00:18:22,681 --> 00:18:25,220
began to arrive in Vietnam.

341
00:18:25,221 --> 00:18:30,800
By the end of 1967, they would number 17,000 strong.

342
00:18:30,801 --> 00:18:33,720
Their mission was to eliminate the Viet Cong,

343
00:18:33,721 --> 00:18:38,920
destroy their subterranean stronghold, and protect Saigon.

344
00:18:38,921 --> 00:18:42,700
The 25th set up three camps, each bordering the treacherous

345
00:18:42,701 --> 00:18:46,900
Iron Triangle, Boiloi, and Hobo Woods.

346
00:18:46,901 --> 00:18:49,640
The main base at Ku Chi gave them quick access

347
00:18:49,641 --> 00:18:52,280
to these danger zones.

348
00:18:52,281 --> 00:18:55,200
Strategic planners, however, soon realized that they had made

349
00:18:55,201 --> 00:18:56,500
a fatal error.

350
00:18:56,501 --> 00:19:03,420
The 25th began taking fire inside the Ku Chi base camp.

351
00:19:03,421 --> 00:19:07,460
We had three tunnels under 25th Division's base camp.

352
00:19:07,461 --> 00:19:09,520
They were built before they arrived.

353
00:19:09,521 --> 00:19:13,860
When we attacked, they were taken by surprise.

354
00:19:13,861 --> 00:19:18,120
The 25th Infantry used earthmovers, called Rome Plows,

355
00:19:18,121 --> 00:19:22,720
and explosives to destroy the tunnels under the base.

356
00:19:22,721 --> 00:19:24,920
It took them months, but eventually,

357
00:19:24,921 --> 00:19:27,700
they were satisfied that they had eliminated the threat

358
00:19:27,701 --> 00:19:29,900
from within.

359
00:19:29,901 --> 00:19:32,280
Military planners were now just beginning

360
00:19:32,281 --> 00:19:35,280
the extent of the tunnel problem.

361
00:19:35,380 --> 00:19:37,460
Despite the best efforts of the tunnel rats,

362
00:19:37,560 --> 00:19:40,220
who destroyed dozens of enemy bunkers and tunnels,

363
00:19:40,320 --> 00:19:43,960
the Viet Cong expanded their system.

364
00:19:44,060 --> 00:19:49,860
By 1967, the tunnel network reached into Saigon itself.

365
00:19:49,960 --> 00:19:53,340
The apex of the complex was literally in the Saigon

366
00:19:53,440 --> 00:19:54,240
suburbs.

367
00:19:54,340 --> 00:19:56,900
It would sort of been like if the Germans would have had a tunnel

368
00:19:57,000 --> 00:20:00,040
going into London in 1940.

369
00:20:00,041 --> 00:20:04,040
Incredibly, even the commander of all Viet Cong forces,

370
00:20:04,140 --> 00:20:07,040
the leader of the resistance fighters in South Vietnam,

371
00:20:07,140 --> 00:20:10,780
Tran Bac Dang, would direct guerrilla operations by night

372
00:20:10,880 --> 00:20:14,880
and slip into Saigon and operate undetected during the day.

373
00:20:17,700 --> 00:20:19,700
I lived half my life in Saigon

374
00:20:19,800 --> 00:20:23,900
and half my life in the tunnels.

375
00:20:24,000 --> 00:20:27,400
My house was next door to the American ambassadors.

376
00:20:30,040 --> 00:20:34,440
On January 10, 1967, the 25th Infantry Division

377
00:20:34,540 --> 00:20:37,640
launched Operation Cedar Falls.

378
00:20:37,740 --> 00:20:42,020
The goal was to trap and crush the Viet Cong dug in and under

379
00:20:42,120 --> 00:20:44,120
the Iron Triangle.

380
00:20:44,220 --> 00:20:48,520
Newly recruited 25th Trooper C.W. Bowman arrived in Vietnam

381
00:20:48,620 --> 00:20:52,300
a few days before he went into the killing zone.

382
00:20:52,400 --> 00:20:53,800
When you were over there, you just

383
00:20:53,900 --> 00:20:57,160
had to reside to the fact that you were going to die.

384
00:20:57,260 --> 00:20:59,040
You know, you probably weren't going to make it,

385
00:20:59,041 --> 00:21:00,740
so you're going to do the best you could,

386
00:21:00,840 --> 00:21:03,140
fight as hard as you could.

387
00:21:03,240 --> 00:21:06,040
Patrol comrade Gary Heater was never too far

388
00:21:06,140 --> 00:21:09,380
from his close friend, Bowman.

389
00:21:09,480 --> 00:21:11,480
You know, I kind of want to get attached to somebody

390
00:21:11,580 --> 00:21:13,080
so I can have a friend over there.

391
00:21:13,180 --> 00:21:16,260
And I didn't want to get too friendly to too many people

392
00:21:16,360 --> 00:21:20,060
in case, you know, you get hurt or lose somebody.

393
00:21:20,160 --> 00:21:23,600
But he's the only one I really got close to.

394
00:21:23,700 --> 00:21:26,040
Incoming troops were filled with tales

395
00:21:26,041 --> 00:21:30,540
of the horrors faced by a small band of men, the tunnel rats,

396
00:21:30,640 --> 00:21:33,480
who dared to chase the fierce Viet Cong down

397
00:21:33,580 --> 00:21:35,680
into their tunnels.

398
00:21:35,780 --> 00:21:38,480
Sometimes they would put right underneath the entrance,

399
00:21:38,580 --> 00:21:42,500
they'd put a man trap, a large punji pit.

400
00:21:42,600 --> 00:21:44,800
Instead of landing on solid ground,

401
00:21:44,900 --> 00:21:48,800
you'd land into a punji pit.

402
00:21:48,900 --> 00:21:51,500
Operation Cedar Falls marked the initiation

403
00:21:51,600 --> 00:21:54,200
of a new breed of tunnel rat.

404
00:21:54,201 --> 00:21:56,100
So many tunnels were being uncovered,

405
00:21:56,200 --> 00:21:59,000
and no time to wait for engineers to search them.

406
00:21:59,100 --> 00:22:02,680
The petrifying task was now open to regular foot soldiers

407
00:22:02,780 --> 00:22:05,480
gutsy enough to volunteer.

408
00:22:05,580 --> 00:22:07,480
In our unit, you know, it was, hey, you know,

409
00:22:07,580 --> 00:22:09,780
we need somebody to go in the tunnel, and we went.

410
00:22:09,880 --> 00:22:13,480
You know, and we took a .45 and chambered around

411
00:22:13,580 --> 00:22:17,460
and cocked the hammer back and went in.

412
00:22:17,560 --> 00:22:21,960
Bowman and Heater volunteered for tunnel rat duty together.

413
00:22:21,961 --> 00:22:24,960
CW and I, we're closer than brothers.

414
00:22:24,961 --> 00:22:28,960
And I'd go in a lot of tunnels, and he'd come in behind me,

415
00:22:28,961 --> 00:22:30,960
or he'd go front.

416
00:22:33,960 --> 00:22:35,960
I felt safe when he was with me.

417
00:22:35,961 --> 00:22:38,960
That's the big thing.

418
00:22:38,961 --> 00:22:42,960
Gary and I, we were just a couple old G.I. Joes, you know,

419
00:22:42,961 --> 00:22:46,960
and looked at us as, I guess, a challenger or whatever,

420
00:22:46,961 --> 00:22:50,960
and stepped up to do it.

421
00:22:50,961 --> 00:22:52,760
Do it.

422
00:22:52,860 --> 00:22:55,640
During Operation Cedar Falls, Bowman and Heater

423
00:22:55,740 --> 00:22:58,300
were initiated in the terrifying hazards of tunnel

424
00:22:58,400 --> 00:22:59,700
rat duty.

425
00:22:59,800 --> 00:23:02,340
He pushed the trap door open, and nothing happened,

426
00:23:02,440 --> 00:23:03,580
you know.

427
00:23:03,680 --> 00:23:06,840
So Gary kind of stuck his arm up there with the light first,

428
00:23:06,940 --> 00:23:09,180
and then just kind of eased up, looked over the edge,

429
00:23:09,280 --> 00:23:10,280
and he dropped back down.

430
00:23:10,380 --> 00:23:12,620
He said, God, this is a buoy trap up there, you know.

431
00:23:12,720 --> 00:23:13,980
And I said, what the hell is up there?

432
00:23:14,080 --> 00:23:15,180
He says, I don't know.

433
00:23:15,280 --> 00:23:16,980
He says, but it doesn't look good, you know.

434
00:23:17,080 --> 00:23:20,960
And we looked back up there, and claimed we were going

435
00:23:20,961 --> 00:23:25,100
was sitting up there on a tripod.

436
00:23:25,200 --> 00:23:28,200
Luckily, the Claymore mine was not booby-trapped,

437
00:23:28,300 --> 00:23:32,400
and Bowman and Heater surfaced safely.

438
00:23:32,500 --> 00:23:36,400
Operation Cedar Falls ended in frustration and failure.

439
00:23:36,500 --> 00:23:38,880
Although some documents, weapons, and ammunition

440
00:23:38,980 --> 00:23:43,920
were recovered, the enemy was far from routed.

441
00:23:44,020 --> 00:23:46,120
The guerrillas quickly and secretively

442
00:23:46,220 --> 00:23:50,120
rebuilt the tunnels that were destroyed.

443
00:23:50,121 --> 00:23:53,120
25th Infantry Tunnel Rats Bowman and Heater

444
00:23:53,220 --> 00:23:56,260
would soon return to action on new operations.

445
00:23:56,360 --> 00:24:01,060
Their biggest fear was meeting the enemy face to face.

446
00:24:01,160 --> 00:24:03,860
In the claustrophobic confines of the tunnel,

447
00:24:03,960 --> 00:24:06,360
the rats knew only one would emerge alive.

448
00:24:09,080 --> 00:24:11,100
Tunnel Rat Gary Heater was shocked

449
00:24:11,200 --> 00:24:14,120
by his first underground encounter.

450
00:24:14,220 --> 00:24:17,020
It turned out to be a three-, four-year-old kid.

451
00:24:17,120 --> 00:24:18,120
This kid was just sitting there.

452
00:24:18,220 --> 00:24:19,620
I guess his dad just left him there,

453
00:24:19,621 --> 00:24:21,420
Maybe he heard me coming.

454
00:24:21,520 --> 00:24:25,560
But I just looked at him, and he looked at me,

455
00:24:25,660 --> 00:24:27,260
and I had a flashlight on him.

456
00:24:27,360 --> 00:24:29,860
And I just kept on going.

457
00:24:29,960 --> 00:24:31,760
It scared me.

458
00:24:31,860 --> 00:24:35,660
He was just a kid, but it could have been daddy.

459
00:24:35,760 --> 00:24:38,480
The one time Bowman went in a tunnel by himself,

460
00:24:38,580 --> 00:24:40,680
he met the real enemy.

461
00:24:40,780 --> 00:24:43,380
He crawled through a long, narrow passageway

462
00:24:43,480 --> 00:24:47,020
that opened up to a large chamber, a recovery room,

463
00:24:47,021 --> 00:24:50,520
with VC guerrillas lying in bunks.

464
00:24:50,620 --> 00:24:53,160
They had, like, their weapons up against the wall and stuff,

465
00:24:53,260 --> 00:24:55,760
and I kind of stumbled in there.

466
00:24:55,860 --> 00:24:58,540
When I came up in there and shined the light, you know,

467
00:24:58,640 --> 00:25:01,740
and boom, it was like Keystone cops.

468
00:25:01,840 --> 00:25:05,740
They started reaching for the weapons, and I started shooting.

469
00:25:05,840 --> 00:25:07,140
Flash, this happens.

470
00:25:07,240 --> 00:25:09,440
Flash, that happens.

471
00:25:09,540 --> 00:25:11,820
People hollering, screaming, people shooting.

472
00:25:11,920 --> 00:25:12,980
Your heart's pounding.

473
00:25:13,080 --> 00:25:15,180
I mean, it's all reaction.

474
00:25:15,181 --> 00:25:16,380
You really don't think.

475
00:25:16,480 --> 00:25:17,780
You just start shooting.

476
00:25:17,880 --> 00:25:19,780
If you hesitate and think about it,

477
00:25:19,880 --> 00:25:22,280
you're the one that's probably going to die.

478
00:25:22,380 --> 00:25:25,920
I shot, you know, and get the hell out of there

479
00:25:26,020 --> 00:25:28,120
as fast as I could.

480
00:25:28,220 --> 00:25:31,700
Bowman remarkably survived this terrifying face-to-face

481
00:25:31,800 --> 00:25:32,700
unscathed.

482
00:25:34,960 --> 00:25:37,440
Yet his tunnel rat buddy Gary Heater

483
00:25:37,540 --> 00:25:39,040
wouldn't be so lucky.

484
00:25:39,140 --> 00:25:41,340
On his last mission before flying home,

485
00:25:41,440 --> 00:25:45,180
he stepped on a landmine known as a bouncing bet.

486
00:25:45,181 --> 00:25:48,780
I knew it was a bouncing batty, because I heard the spring.

487
00:25:48,880 --> 00:25:52,120
As soon as I stepped, we was running through this minefield.

488
00:25:52,220 --> 00:25:53,220
And it went off.

489
00:25:56,520 --> 00:25:58,120
It did knock me unconscious.

490
00:25:58,220 --> 00:26:01,940
I was awake until I got to the hospital.

491
00:26:02,040 --> 00:26:06,540
But I couldn't see my leg.

492
00:26:06,640 --> 00:26:09,040
Gary Heater fortunately survived,

493
00:26:09,140 --> 00:26:11,480
but spent two years in a veteran's hospital

494
00:26:11,580 --> 00:26:14,080
before he could walk again.

495
00:26:14,081 --> 00:26:18,320
As 1967 closed, American military planners

496
00:26:18,420 --> 00:26:19,980
raised the stakes.

497
00:26:20,080 --> 00:26:24,520
B-52 arc light strikes increased in ferocity and breadth.

498
00:26:24,620 --> 00:26:28,020
US planes dropped massive payloads of iron bombs

499
00:26:28,120 --> 00:26:30,460
and chemical defoliants that would eventually

500
00:26:30,560 --> 00:26:33,360
reduce the Iron Triangle and the Hobo Woods

501
00:26:33,460 --> 00:26:36,800
to a desolate moonscape.

502
00:26:36,900 --> 00:26:40,180
Into this milestone, a new crop of America's youth

503
00:26:40,280 --> 00:26:42,140
arrived to do battle.

504
00:26:42,141 --> 00:26:45,040
The bravest volunteered to be tunnel rats.

505
00:26:45,140 --> 00:26:47,840
In the dark depths, they fought for their nation,

506
00:26:47,940 --> 00:26:49,740
their honor, and their lives.

507
00:26:56,380 --> 00:26:58,160
Frustrated with their inability to quell

508
00:26:58,260 --> 00:27:00,360
the dogged Viet Cong resistance,

509
00:27:00,460 --> 00:27:04,200
American military leaders raised the stakes and the heat.

510
00:27:04,300 --> 00:27:08,940
Toward the end of 1967, massive B-52, or arc light,

511
00:27:08,941 --> 00:27:11,980
strikes increased in South Vietnam.

512
00:27:12,040 --> 00:27:14,980
They pounded the Iron Triangle and the surrounding danger

513
00:27:15,040 --> 00:27:15,920
zones.

514
00:27:17,680 --> 00:27:21,680
On the ground, Rome plows were liberally used to unearth

515
00:27:21,760 --> 00:27:24,560
and destroy tunnels.

516
00:27:24,620 --> 00:27:28,160
Chemical defoliants and napalm drops eliminated the jungle

517
00:27:28,220 --> 00:27:30,360
canopy used as cover by the enemy.

518
00:27:33,360 --> 00:27:35,640
Well, by the time all that was done, you defoliated things,

519
00:27:35,700 --> 00:27:38,140
all these holes started popping up all over the place.

520
00:27:38,141 --> 00:27:39,800
And so there was just a lot more holes

521
00:27:39,900 --> 00:27:41,040
than there were tunnel rats, I think.

522
00:27:41,140 --> 00:27:43,280
So they would just say, well, do you want to go down?

523
00:27:43,380 --> 00:27:46,380
And there was always a few of us that would.

524
00:27:46,480 --> 00:27:48,380
The tunnel rats found their own reasons

525
00:27:48,480 --> 00:27:52,080
to justify their dangerous mission.

526
00:27:52,180 --> 00:27:54,080
I enjoyed that mystique.

527
00:27:54,180 --> 00:27:58,100
I enjoyed that whisper when the new guys would come in

528
00:27:58,200 --> 00:28:00,800
and they'd say, that's Corey.

529
00:28:00,900 --> 00:28:02,400
You know, he's crazy.

530
00:28:02,500 --> 00:28:04,900
I hate to admit it, but I loved the rush.

531
00:28:05,000 --> 00:28:07,440
25th Infantryman and tunnel rat

532
00:28:07,441 --> 00:28:09,780
Art Tejeda turned the perilous task

533
00:28:09,880 --> 00:28:12,880
into a high-stakes treasure hunt.

534
00:28:12,980 --> 00:28:14,780
Anything in that tunnel belongs to you,

535
00:28:14,880 --> 00:28:18,080
aside that it going as to intelligence, like maps

536
00:28:18,180 --> 00:28:19,580
and paperwork and stuff like that.

537
00:28:19,680 --> 00:28:21,480
But you find uniforms.

538
00:28:21,580 --> 00:28:25,900
You find weapons, pistols, bolt-action rivals,

539
00:28:26,000 --> 00:28:29,500
and stuff like that, which you can use for barter, which

540
00:28:29,600 --> 00:28:30,900
became pretty good.

541
00:28:31,000 --> 00:28:33,400
And it came to be a good business.

542
00:28:33,401 --> 00:28:36,900
business.

543
00:28:37,000 --> 00:28:38,800
The Viet Cong were ready as ever

544
00:28:38,900 --> 00:28:42,640
to repel interloping tunnel rats.

545
00:28:42,740 --> 00:28:46,480
They would tie pit vipers, and they would hang them upside

546
00:28:46,580 --> 00:28:48,320
down with their tails.

547
00:28:48,420 --> 00:28:51,760
So if you weren't aware of them, and you didn't look close

548
00:28:51,860 --> 00:28:57,400
enough, you stick your head in one of them tunnels, and bang.

549
00:28:57,500 --> 00:29:01,800
I saw one unfortunate young man who was new.

550
00:29:01,900 --> 00:29:03,160
He didn't exactly know what he was doing.

551
00:29:03,161 --> 00:29:04,360
He crawled up.

552
00:29:04,460 --> 00:29:05,600
At least he knew enough to get down.

553
00:29:05,700 --> 00:29:07,600
But he crawled up to the tunnel and looked over the edge.

554
00:29:07,700 --> 00:29:08,800
And he was shot right in the face.

555
00:29:08,900 --> 00:29:11,500
The guy was just sitting right there.

556
00:29:11,600 --> 00:29:13,600
Tragic experience taught the rats

557
00:29:13,700 --> 00:29:16,000
to drop hand grenades into a tunnel entrance

558
00:29:16,100 --> 00:29:17,300
before they went in.

559
00:29:20,420 --> 00:29:23,120
The new rats adopted the now time-honored tools

560
00:29:23,220 --> 00:29:27,320
and techniques of the tunnel rat trailblazers.

561
00:29:27,420 --> 00:29:29,160
Other soldiers would hold me by my ankles

562
00:29:29,260 --> 00:29:31,420
and they'd put me head first.

563
00:29:31,421 --> 00:29:37,820
I'd go in there with a .45, my right hand, flashlight on my left.

564
00:29:37,821 --> 00:29:39,920
Once in the tunnel, the new rats

565
00:29:39,921 --> 00:29:42,300
were prey to the same heart-pounding trials

566
00:29:42,301 --> 00:29:45,900
and tribulations of their predecessors.

567
00:29:45,901 --> 00:29:48,800
25th Infantryman Ken Corey volunteered

568
00:29:48,801 --> 00:29:52,700
to enter and search enemy tunnels.

569
00:29:52,701 --> 00:29:56,280
You were always listening to hear if they were,

570
00:29:56,281 --> 00:29:59,980
you could hear a pin being pulled out of a grenade

571
00:29:59,981 --> 00:30:03,580
or hear a rifle being cocked.

572
00:30:03,680 --> 00:30:06,720
Infantryman Gary Schooler arrived in Vietnam

573
00:30:06,820 --> 00:30:09,320
in October 1967.

574
00:30:09,420 --> 00:30:13,160
Within days, he volunteered to be a tunnel rat.

575
00:30:13,260 --> 00:30:17,560
Memories of his rare duty would last a lifetime.

576
00:30:17,660 --> 00:30:18,760
There's one thing that will give me dreams

577
00:30:18,860 --> 00:30:20,540
and I've had dreams about, and that is the thought

578
00:30:20,640 --> 00:30:24,680
of being buried alive, of being trapped underground,

579
00:30:24,780 --> 00:30:27,900
not being able to get out, and your air slowly running out.

580
00:30:27,901 --> 00:30:31,100
And I never quite overcame that.

581
00:30:31,200 --> 00:30:33,000
I have awoken in the middle of the night

582
00:30:33,100 --> 00:30:35,700
in a cold sweat thinking about that.

583
00:30:35,800 --> 00:30:37,580
During an underground search,

584
00:30:37,680 --> 00:30:39,980
Gary Schooler and his partner got lost

585
00:30:40,080 --> 00:30:43,020
in a deep and dark tunnel system.

586
00:30:43,120 --> 00:30:44,220
Forget the weapons.

587
00:30:44,320 --> 00:30:45,180
We don't care about the glory.

588
00:30:45,280 --> 00:30:47,020
I mean, we just want to get out of there.

589
00:30:47,120 --> 00:30:49,020
And you start thinking about, would I, you know,

590
00:30:49,120 --> 00:30:51,560
could we be lost in here for a long time?

591
00:30:51,660 --> 00:30:53,260
Or maybe never get out.

592
00:30:53,360 --> 00:30:56,420
Finally, it seemed like we'd been down there three hours.

593
00:30:56,421 --> 00:30:58,720
and finally saw a little shaft of light.

594
00:30:58,820 --> 00:31:00,720
We went to it, and it was a well.

595
00:31:00,820 --> 00:31:03,420
Popped out of the ground, and it was in the middle of a clearing.

596
00:31:03,520 --> 00:31:07,060
It was just jungle, 360 degrees all around us.

597
00:31:07,160 --> 00:31:11,760
Gary Schooler and his partner made it out spooked, but safe.

598
00:31:11,860 --> 00:31:14,840
As a rule, however, once the tunnel had been searched

599
00:31:14,940 --> 00:31:17,400
and all intelligence and arms recovered,

600
00:31:17,500 --> 00:31:21,140
the tunnel rats had to go back down and destroy it.

601
00:31:21,240 --> 00:31:23,780
First, they would plant the C4 explosives

602
00:31:23,880 --> 00:31:25,920
in the most effective spots, then

603
00:31:25,921 --> 00:31:29,520
to coordinate the demolition with the engineers detonating

604
00:31:29,620 --> 00:31:30,520
the charge.

605
00:31:32,720 --> 00:31:33,660
And they said, are we ready?

606
00:31:33,760 --> 00:31:35,360
And he said, yeah, OK.

607
00:31:35,460 --> 00:31:37,660
So I'd crawl back down the tunnel toward the end

608
00:31:37,760 --> 00:31:40,960
of the tunnel, and I'd pull the fuses.

609
00:31:41,060 --> 00:31:42,980
And this would start the cord.

610
00:31:43,080 --> 00:31:45,880
And as I'm crawling back, I'd be pulling fuses

611
00:31:45,980 --> 00:31:47,580
on every satchel.

612
00:31:47,680 --> 00:31:50,020
Once I got to the opening, they'd haul me out,

613
00:31:50,120 --> 00:31:52,280
and we'd run like heck.

614
00:31:52,281 --> 00:31:55,180
And the ground would go up.

615
00:31:55,280 --> 00:31:57,520
The ground would go down.

616
00:31:57,620 --> 00:31:59,420
End of tunnel.

617
00:31:59,520 --> 00:32:02,920
Tragically, Art Tejeda lost his partner, John Riley,

618
00:32:03,020 --> 00:32:07,960
and nearly died himself in a terrifying tunnel search.

619
00:32:08,060 --> 00:32:09,760
Flashlight pointed down the tunnel,

620
00:32:09,860 --> 00:32:15,440
and there were three VC there looking straight at us.

621
00:32:15,540 --> 00:32:20,140
And they opened up.

622
00:32:20,141 --> 00:32:27,140
And the next thing I saw was this green, yellow, red color

623
00:32:27,141 --> 00:32:30,140
flash, loud bang.

624
00:32:30,141 --> 00:32:35,140
Got my .45 and pointed it down the tunnel

625
00:32:35,141 --> 00:32:38,140
and emptied out the clip.

626
00:32:38,141 --> 00:32:42,140
I didn't hear any more, any more sounds or anything.

627
00:32:42,141 --> 00:32:47,140
I tried to get John, and he wasn't moving.

628
00:32:47,141 --> 00:32:48,940
And I put my hand on his chest.

629
00:32:49,040 --> 00:32:53,040
His heart wasn't pounding or pumping anyway.

630
00:32:53,140 --> 00:32:54,540
He was dead.

631
00:32:56,640 --> 00:32:58,880
Art Tejeda was hit in the side.

632
00:32:58,980 --> 00:33:02,880
He was losing lots of blood and strength.

633
00:33:02,980 --> 00:33:06,700
And I could see my mother's face so lifelike.

634
00:33:06,800 --> 00:33:08,900
And she told me, I says, Art, you're hurt.

635
00:33:09,000 --> 00:33:10,500
Get out of that tunnel.

636
00:33:10,600 --> 00:33:12,400
I said, no, I'm tired.

637
00:33:12,500 --> 00:33:14,100
And she said, damn you, Art.

638
00:33:14,200 --> 00:33:17,140
Get up and see the sun for one minute.

639
00:33:17,141 --> 00:33:19,440
last time.

640
00:33:19,441 --> 00:33:21,640
So I started crawling out.

641
00:33:21,641 --> 00:33:23,480
I was just so sleepy, so tired.

642
00:33:23,481 --> 00:33:25,640
I felt comfortable.

643
00:33:25,641 --> 00:33:27,680
I wasn't hurting.

644
00:33:27,681 --> 00:33:34,600
Consequently, I saw a light and got myself out of that tunnel.

645
00:33:34,601 --> 00:33:44,440
And that was one of my scariest days in Vietnam.

646
00:33:44,441 --> 00:33:47,200
Tunnel rats John Riley and Art Tejeda

647
00:33:47,201 --> 00:33:49,300
had been victims of an ominous buildup

648
00:33:49,301 --> 00:33:51,780
in Viet Cong tunnel activity.

649
00:33:51,781 --> 00:33:56,060
As 1968 arrived, tunnel rats found more and more stockpiles

650
00:33:56,061 --> 00:33:59,760
of arms and munitions.

651
00:33:59,761 --> 00:34:02,440
It was very common to find a cache

652
00:34:02,441 --> 00:34:04,240
with maybe 30, 40 weapons.

653
00:34:04,241 --> 00:34:05,780
Why were all these supplies?

654
00:34:05,781 --> 00:34:07,100
For what? There's nothing out there.

655
00:34:07,101 --> 00:34:08,540
You know, it's the Iron Triangle.

656
00:34:08,541 --> 00:34:10,340
It's a raised desert.

657
00:34:10,341 --> 00:34:11,180
It's a moonscape.

658
00:34:11,181 --> 00:34:13,540
What is all this stuff doing there?

659
00:34:13,541 --> 00:34:17,180
By the end of January 1968, the real reason

660
00:34:17,181 --> 00:34:20,300
for the huge arms caches and underground enemy encounters

661
00:34:20,301 --> 00:34:21,780
would be unveiled.

662
00:34:21,781 --> 00:34:25,520
The Viet Cong were about to deliver a stunning hammer blow

663
00:34:25,521 --> 00:34:30,000
on American and Arvin forces in every city in South Vietnam

664
00:34:30,001 --> 00:34:31,280
at once.

665
00:34:31,281 --> 00:34:34,600
It would forever be remembered as the Tet Offensive.

666
00:34:37,280 --> 00:34:39,540
Some tunnels were so deep, they were

667
00:34:39,541 --> 00:34:42,160
immune to the B-52 strikes.

668
00:34:42,161 --> 00:34:44,800
Close to half of the communist troops in the tunnels

669
00:34:44,801 --> 00:34:48,560
survived the attacks, while few survived on the outside.

670
00:34:52,140 --> 00:34:56,040
On January 31st, 1968, the Viet Cong

671
00:34:56,041 --> 00:34:59,440
and the North Vietnamese Army launched the Tet Offensive.

672
00:35:05,120 --> 00:35:08,900
In one single massive blow, they hit every major city

673
00:35:08,901 --> 00:35:11,560
in South Vietnam at the same time.

674
00:35:11,561 --> 00:35:14,200
The communists believed the South Vietnamese army

675
00:35:14,201 --> 00:35:17,200
would crumble and the people in the cities would rise up

676
00:35:17,201 --> 00:35:19,700
and join them.

677
00:35:19,701 --> 00:35:22,300
The formidable 9th Viet Cong Division,

678
00:35:22,301 --> 00:35:24,840
the guerrillas who built and fought so tenaciously

679
00:35:24,841 --> 00:35:29,580
from the tunnels around Cu Chi, were joined by units of the NVA

680
00:35:29,581 --> 00:35:32,920
and attacked Saigon.

681
00:35:32,921 --> 00:35:36,420
The true reason for the huge caches of arms and supplies

682
00:35:36,421 --> 00:35:40,320
uncovered by the tunnel rats had been revealed.

683
00:35:40,321 --> 00:35:43,060
January 31st, when the Tet Offensive hit,

684
00:35:43,160 --> 00:35:45,460
it all became clear, because that was a staging area.

685
00:35:45,560 --> 00:35:47,860
The troops moved in there in something like two or three

686
00:35:47,960 --> 00:35:50,060
days, and through the tunnels, they picked up their weapons,

687
00:35:50,160 --> 00:35:52,260
all their gear, and all this ammunition stuff

688
00:35:52,360 --> 00:35:53,360
had been stockpiled.

689
00:35:58,780 --> 00:36:01,180
The undefeated 9th Viet Cong Division

690
00:36:01,280 --> 00:36:03,280
and units of the North Vietnamese Army

691
00:36:03,380 --> 00:36:06,480
sprang from the tunnels and attacked Saigon.

692
00:36:06,481 --> 00:36:12,520
They were led by Vietnamese war hero, Tran Bac Dang.

693
00:36:12,620 --> 00:36:15,120
The tunnels serve as the staging area.

694
00:36:15,220 --> 00:36:18,420
We launched a Tet Offensive from there.

695
00:36:18,520 --> 00:36:20,960
America's 1st and 25th divisions

696
00:36:21,060 --> 00:36:23,460
and the South Vietnamese Army, after years

697
00:36:23,560 --> 00:36:27,740
of frustrating guerrilla warfare, swiftly engaged the enemy.

698
00:36:27,840 --> 00:36:32,180
The morale in most American combat units actually went up.

699
00:36:32,280 --> 00:36:33,880
Here you've got an objective.

700
00:36:33,980 --> 00:36:35,880
The enemy is there.

701
00:36:35,881 --> 00:36:36,780
They're out there.

702
00:36:36,880 --> 00:36:39,480
They're fighting.

703
00:36:39,580 --> 00:36:43,180
26 days later, the attack on Saigon and South Vietnam

704
00:36:43,280 --> 00:36:45,020
was repelled.

705
00:36:45,120 --> 00:36:48,220
Thousands of Viet Cong and NVA were killed,

706
00:36:48,320 --> 00:36:52,060
and the 9th Viet Cong Division was completely decimated.

707
00:36:52,160 --> 00:36:55,400
Tens of thousands are thought to have died.

708
00:36:55,500 --> 00:36:57,940
The Tet Offensive had failed for the Viet Cong

709
00:36:58,040 --> 00:37:00,740
in its military objectives.

710
00:37:00,840 --> 00:37:03,400
In the wake of Tet, American military leaders

711
00:37:03,401 --> 00:37:05,200
leaders redoubled their attacks.

712
00:37:05,300 --> 00:37:09,040
B-52 bomb strikes aimed directly on the Iron Triangle,

713
00:37:09,140 --> 00:37:11,040
and the underground fortifications

714
00:37:11,140 --> 00:37:13,440
increased in ferocity.

715
00:37:13,540 --> 00:37:18,140
The first thing you would see is these flashes, but no sound.

716
00:37:18,240 --> 00:37:21,260
And then you'd feel the rumble of the ground.

717
00:37:21,360 --> 00:37:23,060
The ground starts running like an earthquake.

718
00:37:23,160 --> 00:37:25,060
Then the next thing, the last thing,

719
00:37:25,160 --> 00:37:26,260
is the sound finally gets to you.

720
00:37:29,500 --> 00:37:32,560
In my opinion, the sound of the bombs falling

721
00:37:32,561 --> 00:37:36,060
was more frightening than the sound of the explosion.

722
00:37:40,800 --> 00:37:44,360
The bombs exploding two kilometers away

723
00:37:44,361 --> 00:37:45,580
were the most dangerous.

724
00:37:46,140 --> 00:37:49,460
The air pressure and where it caused was so strong

725
00:37:49,461 --> 00:37:52,400
would bury people trying to escape from the tunnel.

726
00:37:52,401 --> 00:38:06,401
I fought many American soldiers, not only in Coochie, but in many places, face to face.

727
00:38:08,320 --> 00:38:09,860
I'm not sure how I survived.

728
00:38:10,560 --> 00:38:12,380
Perhaps it was the will of God.

729
00:38:15,700 --> 00:38:20,580
The few Viet Cong fighters that survived the Tet Offensive and the B-52 strikes

730
00:38:20,581 --> 00:38:22,320
soon abandoned the tunnel.

731
00:38:22,400 --> 00:38:27,400
Instead of 20 men, 20-man cells protecting a certain part

732
00:38:27,500 --> 00:38:30,400
of the tunnel complex, they were down to two or three men.

733
00:38:30,500 --> 00:38:33,440
And that was kind of the beginning of the infront of

734
00:38:33,540 --> 00:38:34,640
the tunnels.

735
00:38:34,740 --> 00:38:37,640
There weren't enough people to fix the damage.

736
00:38:37,740 --> 00:38:41,060
The Viet Cong began to pull back from the Iron Triangle

737
00:38:41,160 --> 00:38:44,560
in Hobo Woods toward Cambodia and the north.

738
00:38:44,660 --> 00:38:48,060
Some gorilla cells retreated into caves secreted in the Black

739
00:38:48,160 --> 00:38:49,060
Lady Mountain.

740
00:38:49,061 --> 00:38:54,060
Despite the best efforts of the rats sent to destroy the Viet Cong

741
00:38:54,061 --> 00:38:58,060
mountain fortification, the guerrillas and NVA fighters held

742
00:38:58,061 --> 00:39:00,060
the mountain for the duration of the war.

743
00:39:00,061 --> 00:39:03,060
We had the top, we had the bottom, we had the middle.

744
00:39:03,061 --> 00:39:04,060
But it was impenetrable.

745
00:39:04,061 --> 00:39:07,060
It was one of those impenetrable fortresses, and we never did.

746
00:39:07,061 --> 00:39:09,060
We never could drive them out of there.

747
00:39:09,061 --> 00:39:10,060
It was a safe haven for them.

748
00:39:10,061 --> 00:39:15,060
In 1968, 14,000 American troops died in South Vietnam.

749
00:39:15,061 --> 00:39:18,060
It was the worst time in the war.

750
00:39:18,061 --> 00:39:21,800
It was the worst year for casualties on all sides.

751
00:39:21,900 --> 00:39:24,600
While accurate statistics are not available,

752
00:39:24,700 --> 00:39:27,400
some experts estimate dozens of infantrymen

753
00:39:27,500 --> 00:39:30,800
lost their lives on tunnel rat missions.

754
00:39:30,900 --> 00:39:33,980
For the dutiful line soldiers and courageous tunnel rats

755
00:39:34,080 --> 00:39:38,020
who survived, the flight home was a victory.

756
00:39:38,120 --> 00:39:40,320
Oh, going home.

757
00:39:40,420 --> 00:39:43,760
The Freedom Bird, that's what we used to call that last flight

758
00:39:43,860 --> 00:39:45,060
out of the country.

759
00:39:45,160 --> 00:39:46,360
And you can imagine.

760
00:39:46,361 --> 00:39:48,160
You're out here with a rifle.

761
00:39:48,260 --> 00:39:50,300
You're sloshing in a stupid rice paddy.

762
00:39:50,400 --> 00:39:51,600
You got all this stench.

763
00:39:51,700 --> 00:39:53,360
You got the bugs.

764
00:39:53,460 --> 00:39:54,800
And here you're looking at a plane.

765
00:39:54,900 --> 00:39:57,500
You say, gee, I hope it's my turn next.

766
00:40:01,700 --> 00:40:05,120
Today, statues of revolutionary leader Ho Chi Minh

767
00:40:05,220 --> 00:40:07,920
stand in the streets of Saigon.

768
00:40:08,020 --> 00:40:11,020
The bustling former capital of South Vietnam

769
00:40:11,120 --> 00:40:16,360
is now district one of the newly named Ho Chi Minh City.

770
00:40:16,361 --> 00:40:20,360
Only 40 miles north lay the tunnels of Cu Chi.

771
00:40:20,460 --> 00:40:24,360
They are now open to the public as a war memorial,

772
00:40:24,460 --> 00:40:26,360
administered by veteran Viet Cong guerrillas.

773
00:40:29,500 --> 00:40:32,360
As American soldiers searched above,

774
00:40:32,460 --> 00:40:34,360
the Viet Cong hit below.

775
00:40:34,460 --> 00:40:37,360
We had tunnels right here.

776
00:40:37,460 --> 00:40:41,360
The tunnels of Cu Chi, the underground fortification

777
00:40:41,460 --> 00:40:44,360
that was at the heart of the Viet Cong victory,

778
00:40:44,361 --> 00:40:47,000
is celebrated as a national monument,

779
00:40:47,100 --> 00:40:50,300
as significant as Boston is to the American Revolution.

780
00:40:54,140 --> 00:40:57,100
Koo Chi served not only as a battlefront,

781
00:40:57,200 --> 00:41:00,000
but a symbol of self-determination.

782
00:41:00,100 --> 00:41:02,120
It gave the Vietnamese people courage

783
00:41:02,220 --> 00:41:04,020
to fight the American soldiers.

784
00:41:08,120 --> 00:41:10,920
Colonel Chow Lam was an artillery officer

785
00:41:11,020 --> 00:41:12,960
with the 9th Viet Cong Division

786
00:41:12,961 --> 00:41:15,620
and fought from these underground bunkers.

787
00:41:20,640 --> 00:41:22,380
This is a fighting post.

788
00:41:22,860 --> 00:41:25,800
In the over 250 kilometers of tunnel,

789
00:41:26,300 --> 00:41:28,580
there were thousands of these fighting posts.

790
00:41:35,080 --> 00:41:38,240
Adventurous visitors are free to explore the Viet Cong's

791
00:41:38,241 --> 00:41:40,660
once-secret underground bunkers and tunnels.

792
00:41:42,960 --> 00:41:45,720
This is a trap door.

793
00:41:45,721 --> 00:41:49,200
Even if they found it, it was armed with a booby trap.

794
00:41:49,201 --> 00:41:52,720
If American soldiers tried to open it, it would explode.

795
00:41:52,721 --> 00:41:54,960
It could only be opened from the inside.

796
00:41:54,961 --> 00:41:57,600
Anyone who tries to open it from the outside

797
00:41:57,601 --> 00:42:00,400
would be killed in the explosion.

798
00:42:00,401 --> 00:42:04,560
Also on display, a grisly array of simple booby traps.

799
00:42:04,561 --> 00:42:07,520
Cleverly crafted and cunningly placed,

800
00:42:07,521 --> 00:42:10,400
these contraptions were designed to maim.

801
00:42:10,401 --> 00:42:14,000
These contraptions were designed to maim.

802
00:42:14,100 --> 00:42:16,940
The horrifically wounded troopers would require help,

803
00:42:17,040 --> 00:42:19,740
medics, and helicopters.

804
00:42:19,840 --> 00:42:23,680
A whole company could be tied up and be vulnerable to attack.

805
00:42:23,780 --> 00:42:26,320
The stunning simplicity of these booby traps

806
00:42:26,420 --> 00:42:31,220
is a grim reminder of the brutality of war.

807
00:42:31,320 --> 00:42:33,520
This is where we brought injured soldiers

808
00:42:33,620 --> 00:42:36,300
after they had been administered surgery.

809
00:42:36,400 --> 00:42:39,000
The Ku Chi fighters were treated here,

810
00:42:39,001 --> 00:42:41,460
And our doctors and nurses saved many lives

811
00:42:41,560 --> 00:42:43,740
in a very difficult situation.

812
00:42:46,740 --> 00:42:49,640
In the nightmare that was the Vietnam War,

813
00:42:49,740 --> 00:42:52,580
the troops in the combat zone distinguish themselves

814
00:42:52,680 --> 00:42:57,220
with their commitment to duty, honor, and country.

815
00:42:57,320 --> 00:43:00,160
The tunnel rats of America's fighting forces,

816
00:43:00,260 --> 00:43:02,960
including the 1st and 25th Divisions,

817
00:43:03,060 --> 00:43:05,360
and Australia's three field troop,

818
00:43:05,361 --> 00:43:08,800
showed uncommon valor and nerves of steel

819
00:43:08,900 --> 00:43:11,160
as they dared to chase the enemy down

820
00:43:11,260 --> 00:43:13,860
into the dreadful, dark passageways.

821
00:43:13,960 --> 00:43:15,940
They recovered intelligence and arms

822
00:43:16,040 --> 00:43:18,600
that stemmed the tide of enemy insurgents

823
00:43:18,700 --> 00:43:20,500
and helped save lives.

824
00:43:20,600 --> 00:43:23,180
In the black, petrifying passageways,

825
00:43:23,280 --> 00:43:26,040
the tunnel rats disarmed lethal booby traps

826
00:43:26,140 --> 00:43:28,580
and met the enemy face to face.

827
00:43:28,680 --> 00:43:32,420
The lucky and quick lived to tell the tale.

828
00:43:32,520 --> 00:43:35,360
It's the idea that you can overcome that fear.

829
00:43:35,361 --> 00:43:38,660
There's nothing like going through that kind of thing and winning.

830
00:43:39,760 --> 00:43:42,200
I mean, bad things can happen to you, but if you come out ahead,

831
00:43:43,100 --> 00:43:44,500
you've got something to be proud of, I think.

832
00:43:45,480 --> 00:43:47,900
I really enjoyed the minute I got out.

833
00:43:48,340 --> 00:43:52,940
That was the best part of the mission, was getting out of that hole.

834
00:43:55,760 --> 00:43:58,920
I didn't consider myself a hero or anything like that.

835
00:43:59,060 --> 00:44:01,640
I was just a grunt like the rest of them.

836
00:44:02,060 --> 00:44:04,840
I've always, the guys that didn't make it and stuff,

837
00:44:04,841 --> 00:44:06,940
You know, they were the heroes.

838
00:44:06,941 --> 00:44:10,440
We were just GI Joes, you know, doing our job.

